chx:F1 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Background"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Chapter 21 of the 3rd edition teaches colors as RGBA tuples with Pillow's ImageColor.getcolor() and a table of eight color names; pixel coordinates with the origin at the top left and box tuples of left, top, right and bottom; Pillow images through Image.open(), Image.new(), size, format, save(), crop(), copy(), paste(), resize(), rotate(), transpose(), getpixel() and putpixel(); Project 16, a script that shrinks images into a 300 pixel square and pastes a logo in the corner; the ImageDraw module with points, lines, rectangles, ellipses, polygons and text, and ImageFont.truetype(); the pyperclipimg package for the clipboard; and Matplotlib line graphs, scatter plots, bar graphs and pie charts, with markers, colors, labels, a legend and a grid; it closes with 12 practice questions and 3 practice programs." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01 .
chx:F2 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter's Table 21-1 and its text give green as (0, 255, 0, 255), but ImageColor.getcolor('green', 'RGBA') returns (0, 128, 0, 255) in Pillow 12.3.0, and (0, 255, 0, 255) is the name lime; the other seven names of the table, red, blue, white, black, gray, yellow and purple, return exactly the tuples printed, and the chapter's 'chocolate', 'CornflowerBlue' and case-insensitive 'RED' also hold; the list of names has 148 entries, which the chapter calls more than 100 and the documentation some 140." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03 .
chx:F3 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Most of the chapter's Pillow shell sessions reproduce with generated images of the same sizes: crop() gives 230 by 215, resize() gives half sizes and height plus 300, the tile loops visit 24 positions from (0, 0) to (690, 1075), getpixel() and putpixel() give (0, 0, 0, 0), (210, 210, 210, 255) and (169, 169, 169, 255), the drawing example paints the blue rectangle of 41 by 31 pixels, and the logo program gives a 225 by 300 picture; but saving an RGBA image to a .jpg file raises OSError: cannot write mode RGBA as JPEG, so the chapter's save('zophie.jpg') works only because that picture has no alpha channel, which the chapter does not say." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P06, chx:P07 .
chx:F4 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The chapter says that rotated images are filled with a black background on Windows and with transparent pixels on macOS and Linux; executed on Linux, the fill followed the image mode instead, (0, 0, 0, 0) for an RGBA image and (0, 0, 0) for an RGB one, a fillcolor argument sets it, and expand=True with 90 degrees needs no fill; the chapter also says Pillow writes PNG files at 72 pixels per inch by default, but a saved PNG carried no resolution at all until dpi=(72, 72) was given; and it calls the font size of ImageFont.truetype() points, where the documentation says pixels." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P05 .
chx:F5 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "The code printed for Step 4 of Project 16 writes the subtraction with an en dash (the page source holds the HTML entity for it), so pasting it raises SyntaxError: invalid character '–' (U+2013); the program's test, width and height both over 300, leaves a 1000 by 200 strip unresized although the text says to reduce whichever side is larger; its proportion int((300 / height) * width) gives 224 and not 225 for a 318 by 424 picture because the float product is 224.99999999999997; endswith('.jpg') skips photo.JPG; and os.listdir() returns names in arbitrary order, so the lines it prints need not come in the chapter's order." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P13 .
chx:F6 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Comparative analysis"@en ; sen0414:findingText "For Matplotlib, plt.plot() returns a list of one Line2D, plt.scatter() a PathCollection and plt.bar() a BarContainer as the chapter prints, but since Matplotlib 3.11 plt.pie() returns a PieContainer where the chapter prints a tuple that starts with a list of Wedge objects, although unpacking it into wedges, label texts and percent texts still works; savefig() of the default figure writes a 640 by 480 PNG; and the statement that the image must be saved before show() holds for a blocking window, but under the non-interactive Agg backend show() returned None at once and left the lines in place, so the claims about the closed window were not run." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10 .
chx:F7 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Contemporary developments"@en ; sen0414:findingText "Current practice adds what the chapter leaves out: Image.open() is lazy and keeps the file open until the pixels are read, so a with statement closes it; Image.thumbnail() does in place what the proportion arithmetic of Project 16 does, never enlarges, and gave 225 by 300 for the 318 by 424 case; the documentation spells the flip options as Image.Transpose.FLIP_LEFT_RIGHT while the old Image.FLIP_LEFT_RIGHT still works and compares equal; Image.open() raises UnidentifiedImageError for a file that is not an image, which the photo folder practice program must handle; ImageFont.load_default(size) gives a font where arial.ttf cannot be found; and Matplotlib's explicit interface, fig, ax = plt.subplots(), keeps the figure in a variable instead of in the hidden state that plt functions use." ; sen0414:cites chx:P02, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P11 .
chx:F8 a sen0414:Finding ; rdfs:label "Conclusion"@en ; sen0414:findingText "For an advanced course, chapter 21 is best taught by asking of each Pillow call whether it returns a new image (crop, copy, resize, rotate, transpose), changes its image in place and returns None (paste, putpixel, thumbnail, the ImageDraw methods), or only reads (getpixel, size); the tuples of the coordinate system and of the box decide what is selected, with crop and paste stopping before the right and bottom and a drawn rectangle including them; the chapter's outputs hold with Pillow 12.3.0 and Matplotlib 3.11.2 except the color green, the en dash in Step 4, the pie return value and the statements on rotation fill, resolution and font size, and the standard-library models of this document (a grid of pixels, box arithmetic, tile positions, fitting and alpha mixing) reproduce Pillow's results without installing it." ; sen0414:cites chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P08 .
chx:Scorecard a sen0414:QualityScorecard ; rdfs:label "Quality scorecard"@en ; sen0414:topicCoverage "41 primary-source concepts inventoried from the textbook ontology." ; sen0414:citationStrength "15 sources, all opened and verified at 2026-10-01T12:00:00; 12 cited by findings." ; sen0414:methodologyCompliance "RDODI procedure v1.6.0 Stage 1." ; sen0414:reproducibility "Every source is a stable public URL; every claim names its sources." .
